A||||21||Oreif||Detailing Tip (ashtrays)||||6||
Z||000000||Oreif||04-11-2000||02:05 PM||||Here's a tip I took out my ashtrays and using a Dremel tool with a brush bit, I scrubbed the ashtray with rubbing compound. I then used Mother's brand aluminum polish and again scrubbed. Washed with a mild soap and dried! The first pic is the passenger side one the after is the driver side one. (Driver side one looked just like the passenger side before I started)<P>BEFORE<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/before.jpg">  <P>AFTER<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/After.jpg">  <P>Takes about 10 minutes to do! Gotta get the passenger side one clean now!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 04-11-2000).]||||reg||6
Z||000001||TheFiero64||04-11-2000||02:09 PM||||Cool, Great tip. It looks SWEET! I will have to try it now. Where would we be without a dremel  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000002||Old Lar||04-11-2000||07:23 PM||||You can buy new ashtrays part # 61793 from the Fiero Store for $2.95 each.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000003||Oreif||04-11-2000||08:33 PM||||Let's see $5.90 for new ones, $2.00 for shipping, wait 2-3 days...... or just use what is already on the shelf in my garage and spend 20 minutes running a dremel tool. hmmm.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
